  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1... \nA weak cold front will continue to drop southeast across the\nUpper Ohio Valley region this morning, though no rain is \nexpected with a lack of deep layer moisture. The main impact of \nthis front will be increased cloud cover along the front, with \nscattered stratocu in cold advection through the afternoon. \nHighs today should also be around 10 degrees below Thursday's \nreadings. \n\nDry weather is then expected to continue through the weekend as\nsurface high pressure builds across the region. Mid and high\nlevel clouds should gradually increase through this period ahead\nof an approaching shortwave trough across the Midwest.\nTemperatures should moderate again by Sunday, with readings\naround 10 degrees above average.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2...\nA weakening trough is expected to track slowly east across the\nUpper Ohio Valley region Sunday night into Monday. A lack of\nmoisture should be the main limiting factor on seeing any rain\nwith this system, though slight chances POPs were maintained.\nModel ensembles indicate ridging will then build across the\nUpper Ohio Valley region through early Wednesday, ahead of a \ndeepening central CONUS trough. This should maintain dry weather\nand warm temperatures across the area. Rain chances are \nexpected to begin to increase by mid to late week as the trough\nslowly approaches the region, though uncertainty remains in the\nstrength and forward speed of the trough.",
